cl builds `V arr[2]` by calling its own runtime helper, the vector constructor iterator ??_H@YAXPEAX_K1P6APEAX0@Z@Z, and passing it the element constructor; cxx1 emits the loop inline instead - the difference array-of-class.nocl records. Nothing outside the object can tell which was used. What this case is about, the implicit copy assignment beside an operator= over another type, is checked by run.sh on every machine.
